From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll, kernel32: boot environment info classes, UEFI variables, GetFirmwareType

- ntdll NtQuerySystemInformation: SystemFlagsInformation (9, no flags),
  SystemRangeStartInformation (50, 0xffff080000000000 for 64-bit, one past
  the 32-bit user space under wow64), SystemBootEnvironmentInformation (90,
  firmware type Uefi/Bios from /sys/firmware/efi, boot id from the kernel's
  per-boot id) and SystemSecureBootInformation (145, from the SecureBoot
  EFI variable). They fell to the "stub info class" FIXME. The structures
  are added to winternl.h.
- NtQuerySystemEnvironmentValueEx reads UEFI variables from efivars (data
  plus attributes, STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL with the size, variable-not-found,
  STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED on a BIOS machine); names that cannot be a file
  name are simply not found.
- kernel32: GetFirmwareType reports the real firmware type instead of
  "unknown"; GetFirmwareEnvironmentVariableA/W (stubs) work and the Ex
  A/W forms are added, mapping to ERROR_INVALID_FUNCTION,
  ERROR_ENVVAR_NOT_FOUND, ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER and
  ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER. As on Windows, reading takes
  SeSystemEnvironmentPrivilege, enabled (administrators hold it disabled):
  without it NtQuerySystemEnvironmentValueEx is STATUS_PRIVILEGE_NOT_HELD
  (ERROR_PRIVILEGE_NOT_HELD) before anything is read, whatever the host's
  efivars permissions (integrator). Setting variables stays unsupported:
  nothing writes efivars.
- wow64 passes the new classes through; a header change in winternl.h
  rebuilds most of the tree.

